From: Geodesic Research <noreply@geodesicresearch.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(moe): keep a HybridEP handle's dispatched-token count in
 device memory

Without num_permuted_tokens, HybridEP (deep_ep 1.2.1+34152ae) keeps a
dispatch handle's dispatched-token count in pinned host memory
(executor.cu:107), and its permute and unpermute kernels read it from device
code when they start (permute.cu:326, 459). PyTorch's caching host allocator
is not told about those reads, so once the handle is freed it can hand the
block out again while a combine or a backward that reads it is still queued,
and that kernel then runs on a foreign count, over rows past the received
tokens. Under the EP all-to-all overlap this faulted in training: a GPU core
dump put a Warp MMU Fault in unpermute_kernel<512, bf16, float> with its
count at 262,145, where a rank can receive at most 65,536 tokens.

HybridEPDispatch.forward now hands out a handle whose count is a
non-blocking device copy made on the dispatch stream. The host allocator
records that copy and holds the pinned source until it, and so the dispatch
kernels queued before it, have run. The count is already final when the copy
is queued: the blocking path synchronizes the stream in metadata
preprocessing before dispatch_with_permute returns. With num_permuted_tokens
the count is a device tensor already and the handle is passed through
unchanged. No kernel reads the count on the host on the permute path, so the
copy adds no synchronization.

Dependencies: none. It touches only fused_a2a.py, which the EP-overlap port
(upstream #4798 hybrid EP A2A overlap) does not, so it applies to the bare pin
and to the pin with the port applied.

---
diff --git a/megatron/core/transformer/moe/fused_a2a.py b/megatron/core/transformer/moe/fused_a2a.py
index c281c51..22a85a1 100644
--- a/megatron/core/transformer/moe/fused_a2a.py
+++ b/megatron/core/transformer/moe/fused_a2a.py
@@ -350,6 +350,35 @@ def reset_hybrid_ep_buffer():
     _hybrid_ep_buffer = None
 
 
+# Position of the dispatched-token count in a HybridEP dispatch handle, the same in DeepEP's fused
+# and unfused layouts: (sparse_to_dense_map, rdma_to_attn_map, attn_to_rdma_map,
+# num_dispatched_tokens_tensor, ...).
+_HANDLE_DISPATCHED_TOKENS = 3
+
+
+def _with_device_dispatched_tokens(handle: tuple, device: torch.device) -> tuple:
+    '''
+    Return the HybridEP dispatch handle with its dispatched-token count in device memory.
+
+    Without num_permuted_tokens, HybridEP keeps the count in pinned host memory, and its permute
+    and unpermute kernels read it from device code when they start. PyTorch's caching host
+    allocator is not told about those reads: once the handle is freed it can hand the block out
+    again while a combine or backward that reads it is still queued, and that kernel then runs
+    on a foreign count, over rows past the received tokens. A non-blocking copy on the current
+    stream gives every later reader device memory whose reuse follows the stream, and the host
+    allocator holds the pinned source until the copy, and so the dispatch kernels queued before
+    it, have run.
+    '''
+    count = handle[_HANDLE_DISPATCHED_TOKENS]
+    if count.is_cuda:
+        return handle
+    return (
+        handle[:_HANDLE_DISPATCHED_TOKENS]
+        + (count.to(device, non_blocking=True),)
+        + handle[_HANDLE_DISPATCHED_TOKENS + 1 :]
+    )
+
+
 class HybridEPDispatch(torch.autograd.Function):
     '''
     Fused dispatch operation for permute + dispatch a2a + permute using the HybridEP backend
@@ -428,6 +457,7 @@ class HybridEPDispatch(torch.autograd.Function):
             non_blocking=non_blocking,
             **({"fuse_permute_dispatch": fused} if fused else {}),
         )
+        handle = _with_device_dispatched_tokens(handle, x.device)
 
         ctx.handle = handle
         ctx.pad_multiple = pad_multiple
